A record whose file name breaks the `{NNNN}-{slug}.md` shape gets a `filename` finding on line 1;
its content is still checked against the schema, which it passes.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/value/first.md --
---
type: value
title: First
summary: The first value.
kind: value
created_by: owner
created_at: 2026-01-01
updated_at: 2026-01-01
---

Why the project exists.

## In practice

It shows in every run.
-- cmd --
booping specs check
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
vault/value/first.md:1  error  filename  file name is not {NNNN}-{slug}.md
-- stderr --
1 record(s) checked: 1 error(s), 0 warning(s)
